(Refrigerated tortellini is a pasta that arrives already stuffed with cheese. That means) Tj
T*
(you get the effort of making ravioli with the effort of boiling water. A jar of sauce) Tj
T*
(does the rest.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(WHAT YOU'LL NEED) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1 package \(20 oz\) refrigerated cheese tortellini) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1 jar \(24 oz\) marinara sauce) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3 cups baby spinach) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1/2 cup grated Parmesan or shredded mozzarella) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Salt for the water) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(HOW TO MAKE IT) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fill a large pot about two-thirds full with water, add a big pinch of salt, and bring to) Tj
T*
(a boil.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Add the tortellini and cook according to the package, usually 3 to 5 minutes. They're) Tj
T*
(done when they float and feel tender when you bite one.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In the last 30 seconds, toss in the spinach. It'll wilt right in the pot.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Scoop out 1/2 cup of the pasta water with a mug, then drain the tortellini in a) Tj
T*
(colander.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Return the pot to low heat, add the tortellini and sauce, and stir 2 minutes until hot.) Tj
T*
(If it's too thick, add a splash of the pasta water.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Top with cheese and eat.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Even lazier:) Tj
T*
(Skip the spinach. Use sauce and cheese only.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Good to know:) Tj
T*
